---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Kindling" description="Kindling's Phase 0 privacy notice.">
  <article class="legal section-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Draft for validation</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-notice">Last updated August 10, 2026. This is a pre-launch draft and requires legal review before app-store release.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>The prototype keeps the task and suggested step in the current browser tab. They are not placed in analytics events or sent to Kindling. Anonymous interaction events are buffered in your browser for research export.</p>

    <h2>Waitlist email</h2>
    <p>If you join the waitlist, the configured hosted form provider receives your email address so Kindling can send early-access and product updates. The production provider and its retention terms will be named here before the waitlist goes live. You can unsubscribe from any message.</p>

    <h2>Prototype events</h2>
    <p>The prototype records event names, timestamps, a random session identifier, and limited choices such as the session outcome. Events never contain the task or first-step text. By default they remain in local browser storage until you copy them for a research session or clear them.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can clear the prototype's event buffer from the Research mode panel. You can also clear site data through your browser. To request removal from the waitlist, use the unsubscribe link in an email from the hosted provider.</p>

    <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Kindling is a productivity tool. It does not diagnose, monitor, or treat ADHD or any medical condition, and it is not a substitute for professional care.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
